    "['ip pool [parameter1] bas local', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ip local pool pool1 10.10.10.3 10.10.10.100', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'ip local pool pool1 10.10.10.3 10.10.10.100', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nip local pool pool1 10.10.10.3 10.10.10.100\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. The Huawei \"ip pool\" command creates a local IP address pool for PPP users with the name \"pool1\"\\n2. In Cisco, the equivalent is \"ip local pool\" command\\n3. The main difference is that Cisco requires specifying the start and end IP addresses directly in the pool definition, while Huawei uses a separate \"section\" command\\n4. Note that the gateway and DNS information would need to be configured separately in Cisco (not included in the pool definition)\\n5. The \"bas local\" portion from Huawei isn\\'t needed in Cisco as the \"ip local pool\" command implies this functionality', 'trans_template': 'ip local pool pool1 10.10.10.3 10.10.10.100'}]]": 1,
    "['gateway [parameter1] [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [0, 0], 'trans_command': 'network [parameter1] [parameter2]', 'parent_command': ['ip dhcp pool [parameter1]'], 'root': 'ip dhcp pool [parameter1]'}, {'para_map': [1, 1], 'trans_command': 'network [parameter1] [parameter2]', 'parent_command': ['ip dhcp pool [parameter1]'], 'root': 'ip dhcp pool [parameter1]'}]]": 1,
