    "['[parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'aaa new-model', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'aaa new-model', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\naaa new-model\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\nThe `aaa` command in Huawei devices initiates the AAA (Authentication, Authorization, and Accounting) configuration mode. The equivalent Cisco command is `aaa new-model`, which enables AAA functionality on Cisco routers. Both commands serve as the starting point for configuring authentication, authorization, and accounting services on their respective platforms.', 'trans_template': 'aaa new-model'}]]": 1,
    "['authentication-scheme [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'aaa authentication login default0 group radius', 'parent_command': ['aaa new-model'], 'root': 'aaa new-model', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\naaa authentication login default0 group radius\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Cisco, `authentication-scheme` is translated to `aaa authentication`\\n- The `default0` is kept as the name of the authentication method list\\n- `login` indicates this is for login authentication\\n- `group radius` specifies RADIUS as the authentication method (equivalent to Huawei's default authentication-mode)\\n- Note that Cisco doesn't have direct equivalents for all Huawei authentication scheme options, so this is the closest match for a basic RADIUS authentication scheme.\", 'trans_template': 'aaa authentication login default0 group radius'}]]": 1,
    "['authentication-scheme [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'aaa authentication login default1 group radius', 'parent_command': ['aaa new-model'], 'root': 'aaa new-model', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\naaa authentication login default1 group radius\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Huawei, `authentication-scheme default1` creates an authentication scheme named \"default1\"\\n- The Cisco equivalent is `aaa authentication login` which creates an authentication list\\n- Since the Huawei config later specifies `authentication-mode radius` for this scheme, we use `group radius` in Cisco\\n- The name \"default1\" is preserved as the list name in Cisco', 'trans_template': 'aaa authentication login default1 group radius'}]]": 1,
    "['authentication-scheme [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'aaa authentication ppp auth5 group radius', 'parent_command': ['aaa new-model'], 'root': 'aaa new-model', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\naaa authentication ppp auth5 group radius\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Huawei `authentication-scheme auth5` with `authentication-mode radius` creates a RADIUS authentication method for PPP sessions.\\n- The equivalent Cisco command specifies:\\n  * `aaa authentication ppp` - sets PPP authentication method\\n  * `auth5` - keeps the same profile name\\n  * `group radius` - specifies RADIUS as the authentication method (equivalent to Huawei's radius mode)\", 'trans_template': 'aaa authentication ppp auth5 group radius'}]]": 1,
    "['authentication-mode [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'aaa authentication ppp default group radius', 'parent_command': ['aaa new-model'], 'root': 'aaa new-model', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\naaa authentication ppp default group radius\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\nThe Huawei command `authentication-mode radius` within an authentication scheme configures RADIUS as the authentication method. The equivalent Cisco command sets RADIUS as the authentication method for PPP sessions, using the default RADIUS server group. The `group radius` portion implicitly uses the default RADIUS server configuration in Cisco IOS.', 'trans_template': 'aaa authentication ppp default group radius'}]]": 1,
    "['accounting-scheme [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'aaa accounting default0', 'parent_command': ['aaa new-model'], 'root': 'aaa new-model', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\naaa accounting default0\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Cisco IOS, the `aaa accounting` command is used to define accounting schemes, but the implementation differs slightly from Huawei's approach. Cisco doesn't have an exact 1:1 mapping for Huawei's accounting-scheme context. The above translation represents the closest equivalent concept in Cisco for creating a named accounting scheme. Additional configuration would be needed to specify the accounting methods and servers, similar to how Huawei's configuration continues with `accounting-mode radius`.\", 'trans_template': 'aaa accounting default0'}]]": 1,
    "['accounting-scheme [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'aaa accounting network default1 group radius', 'parent_command': ['aaa new-model'], 'root': 'aaa new-model', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Cisco command for `accounting-scheme default1`:\\n\\n##\\naaa accounting network default1 group radius\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Cisco, this creates a named accounting method \"default1\" that uses RADIUS for network accounting. The Huawei command creates an accounting scheme with default settings (which in this context is RADIUS, as seen in the complete configuration where `accounting-scheme acct5` specifies `accounting-mode radius`).\\n\\nThe Cisco command assumes you want RADIUS accounting since the original Huawei configuration shows RADIUS is being used for accounting schemes (as seen in `accounting-scheme acct5` with `accounting-mode radius`).', 'trans_template': 'aaa accounting network default1 group radius'}]]": 1,
    "['accounting-scheme [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'aaa accounting acct5 group radius', 'parent_command': ['aaa new-model'], 'root': 'aaa new-model', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\naaa accounting acct5 group radius\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Cisco, the equivalent of HUAWEI's `accounting-scheme` configuration is created under the global `aaa` configuration.\\n- The command specifies the accounting method (in this case RADIUS) for the scheme named `acct5`.\\n- Cisco uses `group radius` to indicate RADIUS server group usage, which corresponds to the RADIUS server group (`rd5`) referenced in the HUAWEI configuration.\\n\\nThe translation maintains the same authentication/accounting flow where PPPoE clients will use RADIUS for accounting via the specified scheme.\", 'trans_template': 'aaa accounting acct5 group radius'}]]": 1,
    "['accounting-mode [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'aaa accounting network default group radius', 'parent_command': ['aaa new-model'], 'root': 'aaa new-model', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\naaa accounting network default group radius\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\nThe Huawei `accounting-mode radius` command within an accounting scheme configures RADIUS as the accounting method. The equivalent Cisco command sets RADIUS as the accounting method for network-related services (like PPP) using the default accounting list, which matches the Huawei configuration's intent.\", 'trans_template': 'aaa accounting network default group radius'}]]": 1,
